-- SALT MARSH SAMBA — A minor (all naturals), 74 BPM, 64-cycle form.
-- @scene {"title":"Salt Marsh Samba","cps":0.30833333333333335,"quantize":4}
-- Tempo: cps 0.30833333333333335 = 74 BPM with 1 cycle = one 4/4 bar, so this mixes
-- directly against the existing 74 BPM pair (159 Window Seat / 161 Night Cassette).
-- Key: A natural minor (i-VI-III-VII: Am9 - Fmaj9 - Cmaj9 - G6/9). Every pitch used
-- is a natural, so the later per-channel key alignment has nothing to transpose.
-- Quantize 4: the harmonic cell is four bars (Am-F-C-G) and the drum drop/return
-- lands on four-bar boundaries; starting on a 4-cycle multiple keeps those aligned.
--
-- WHERE THIS CAME FROM (files read in the 50-144 slice, read-only):
--   * 142.tidal SAMPLE-SELECTION SCENE — the two ideas this scene is built on:
--     euclidean rhythm as a rhythm generator (`s "bd(3,8)"` = E(3,8)) and `n` used
--     as real sample selection over a multi-file folder (`n (choose ...)`). Both are
--     re-voiced here on the project's h2ogm acoustic kit and the icshaker bank.
--   * 90.tidal FULL BUILD — the human samba/rhumba one-shot kit (h2ogm* + shaker),
--     and the habit of keeping human drum one-shots on their own lanes with velocity
--     in a gain pattern. The surdo-ish E(3,8) kick and the shaker lane follow it.
--   * 130.tidal TIDAL ESTUARY — independent prime-cycle transformations of peripheral
--     voices (every 5 / 7 / 9 / 11), so layers drift against the bar instead of
--     locking. Here: d4 every 5, d11 every 7, d12 every 9, d10 every 11.
--   * 120.tidal THE CYBERNETIC ORCHESTRA — the "seats" idea (a voice, a machine, a
--     human, a glass) and the high glass bell answering the lead one bar late.
--     d9 is THE VOICE (supersaw with a downward accelerate glide), d10 THE GLASS.
--   * 163.tidal BLUE HOUR — the scene-deck layout itself: six orbits each doing one
--     job, one owner lane per orbit for the orbit-global FX, a swingBy triplet feel,
--     and a gain-0 reset clock on the send orbit. Quantize 4 and the 64-cycle form
--     also follow it.
--   * 100.tidal AMP PATTERNS / SPACE — melodic layers get gain patterns with holes on
--     their own hole-rhythm so the gaps interlock (d8 and d12 here).
--   * 95.tidal REBUILD / 75.tidal SLICK MUFFIN — slice/bite transformations of the
--     LPViz loop bank; d11 slices p93perc with two rotating slice orders.
--   * 159.tidal / 161.tidal (the mix partners) — the two-bar-root / answering-motif
--     bass-and-keys shape at this tempo, and hoRhodes as the project key voice.
-- Recomposition throughout: no tune is quoted, only techniques and one kit are reused.
{- @sc
// One owned writer. Every movement is a function of scene-local cycles.
scene[\mod].value({ |cycles|
    var form    = cycles.mod(64);
    var fracture = (form >= 16) * (form < 40);   // prime-fracture region: layers drift
    var air     = (form >= 40) * (form < 48);    // one distinct drop-out air pocket
    var crest   = (form >= 48) * (form < 60);    // second crest
    var exhale  = form >= 60;
    var arch    = (cycles * (2pi / 64)).sin;
    var tide    = (cycles * (2pi / 8)).sin;
    [5200 + (arch * 1000) - (air * 2400) + (crest * 600) - (exhale * 1800),
     0.10 + (fracture * 0.06) + (crest * 0.04),
     0.10 + (air * 0.16) + (arch * 0.05) + (crest * 0.04),
     0.88 + (tide * 0.035) - (air * 0.07) + (crest * 0.04) - (exhale * 0.08)];
});
-}
-- ORBIT 0 — DRUMS, dry. The master sidechain listens to orbit 0's dry bus, so every
-- lane here keeps the sends at zero and the orbit's own delay/verb/tape muted.
-- d1 THE SURDO: euclidean E(3,8) kick whose sample is chosen from the five-file
-- h2ogmbd bank every four cycles (142's euclid + `n` selection, samba feel from 90).
d1 $ s "h2ogmbd(3,8)" # n (slow 4 $ choose [1,2,3,4]) # orbit 0 # gain "0.95 0.60 0.70" # begin 0 # end 1 # sustain 0.30 # shape 0.4 # hpf 45 # lpf 5600 # pan 0.5 # delaytime 0.1875 # lock 1 # delayfeedback 0 # ddSend 0 # verbSend 0 # room 0 # size 0.3 # verbT60 0.8 # tape 0 # tapeHiss 0
-- d2 THE ANSWERING SNARE: two-bar side-stick / snare / rimshot conversation, swung.
d2 $ swingBy 0.16 8 $ s "<[~ ~ h2ogmsn:3 ~ ~ ~ ~ h2ogmsn:11] [~ h2ogmsn:3 ~ ~ h2ogmsn:7 ~ ~ ~]>" # orbit 0 # gain "<[~ ~ 0.55 ~ ~ ~ ~ 0.72] [~ 0.44 ~ ~ 0.66 ~ ~ ~]>" # begin 0 # end 1 # sustain 0.14 # hpf 220 # lpf 4800 # pan "0.47 0.53" # delaytime 0.1875 # lock 1 # delayfeedback 0 # ddSend 0 # verbSend 0 # room 0 # size 0.3 # verbT60 0.8 # tape 0 # tapeHiss 0
-- d3 THE SWUNG HAT: E(7,16) closed hat, swung, velocity accents per hit.
d3 $ swingBy 0.16 8 $ s "h2ogmhh:2(7,16)" # orbit 0 # gain "0.34 0.18 0.30 0.16 0.28 0.17 0.26" # begin 0 # end 1 # sustain 0.06 # hpf 2200 # lpf 8200 # pan "0.44 0.56" # delaytime 0.1875 # lock 1 # delayfeedback 0 # ddSend 0 # verbSend 0 # room 0 # size 0.3 # verbT60 0.8 # tape 0 # tapeHiss 0
-- d4 THE SHAKER: icshaker E(7,16) with its file picked by `n`; every 5 cycles it doubles.
d4 $ every 5 (fast 2) $ s "icshaker(7,16)" # n "<0 1 4 2>" # orbit 0 # gain "0.24 0.30 0.20 0.28 0.22 0.31 0.19" # begin 0 # end 1 # sustain 0.05 # hpf 1600 # lpf 11000 # pan 0.62 # delaytime 0.1875 # lock 1 # delayfeedback 0 # ddSend 0 # verbSend 0 # room 0 # size 0.3 # verbT60 0.8 # tape 0 # tapeHiss 0
-- ORBIT 1 — BASS, dry. Owner d5. Both lanes share the dry orbit config verbatim.
-- d5 THE FLOOR: dubsub roots a1-f1-c2-g1 with a samba root/octave/fifth cell per bar.
d5 $ n "<[a1 ~ ~ a2 ~ e2 ~ a1] [f1 ~ ~ f2 ~ c2 ~ f1] [c2 ~ ~ c3 ~ g2 ~ c2] [g1 ~ ~ g2 ~ d2 ~ g1]>" # s "dubsub" # orbit 1 # keyShift 0 # amp 0.75 # drive 0.12 # pitchEnv 0 # fenv 2.2 # sustain 0.24 # release 0.18 # hpf 30 # lpf 460 # pan 0.5 # delaytime 0.1875 # lock 1 # delayfeedback 0 # ddSend 0 # verbSend 0 # room 0 # size 0.3 # verbT60 0.8 # tape 0 # tapeHiss 0
-- d6 THE MACHINE: dubsynth riding a rising 3rd/5th line over the same roots, warm.
d6 $ n "<[~ ~ a2 ~ c3 ~ e3 ~] [~ ~ f2 ~ a2 ~ c3 ~] [~ ~ c3 ~ e3 ~ g3 ~] [~ ~ g2 ~ b2 ~ d3 ~]>" # s "dubsynth" # orbit 1 # keyShift 0 # amp 0.6 # waveMix 0.30 # subMix 0.35 # subTone 0.28 # detune 0.05 # fenv 2.0 # cutoff 380 # drive 0.28 # sustain 0.16 # release 0.14 # hpf 34 # lpf 1600 # pan 0.52 # delaytime 0.1875 # lock 1 # delayfeedback 0 # ddSend 0 # verbSend 0 # room 0 # size 0.3 # verbT60 0.8 # tape 0 # tapeHiss 0
-- ORBIT 2 — KEYS into the dub delay. Owner d7; delaytime/feedback/dd*/verb* agree.
-- d7 THE CHORDS: wide rootless Am9 / Fmaj9 / Cmaj9 / G6/9, one per two bars, locked
-- to a dotted-8th (0.1875 cycle) delay (the voicing idea is 163's, re-keyed to Am).
d7 $ slow 2 $ n "<[a3,c4,e4,g4,b4] [f3,a3,c4,e4,g4] [c4,e4,g4,b4,d5] [g3,b3,d4,e4,a4]>" # s "hoRhodes" # orbit 2 # keyShift 0 # gain 0.62 # amp 0.34 # cutoff 3400 # waveMix 0.09 # vib 0.07 # vibRate 4.4 # trem 0.12 # tremRate 3.6 # sustain 1.2 # release 1.6 # pan "0.44 0.56" # delaytime 0.1875 # lock 1 # delayfeedback 0.30 # ddSend 0.34 # ddHp 900 # ddLp 4200 # ddDrive 0.08 # ddWow 0.05 # ddCross 0.60 # ddDuck 0.50 # verbSend 0.10 # room 0.35 # size 0.4 # verbT60 1.6 # verbDamp 0.4 # verbHp 300 # verbLow 0.2 # verbHigh 0.6 # verbTone 4000 # tape 0 # tapeHiss 0
-- d8 THE ANSWER: a sparse hoRhodes motif with interlocking holes (100's amp-hole idea).
d8 $ swingBy 0.12 8 $ n "<[~ ~ e5 ~ a4 ~ c5 ~] [~ ~ c5 ~ a4 ~ ~ ~] [~ ~ e5 ~ g4 ~ a4 ~] [~ ~ d5 ~ ~ b4 ~ ~]>" # s "hoRhodes" # orbit 2 # keyShift 0 # gain "<0 0.55 0 0.42 0 0.5 0 0>" # amp 0.34 # cutoff 2800 # waveMix 0.05 # vib 0.05 # vibRate 4.0 # trem 0.10 # tremRate 3.2 # sustain 0.6 # release 0.7 # pan 0.6 # delaytime 0.1875 # lock 1 # delayfeedback 0.30 # ddSend 0.34 # ddHp 900 # ddLp 4200 # ddDrive 0.08 # ddWow 0.05 # ddCross 0.60 # ddDuck 0.50 # verbSend 0.10 # room 0.35 # size 0.4 # verbT60 1.6 # verbDamp 0.4 # verbHp 300 # verbLow 0.2 # verbHigh 0.6 # verbTone 4000 # tape 0 # tapeHiss 0
-- ORBIT 3 — LEAD + GLASS into the reverb. Owner d9; both lanes share the verb config.
-- d9 THE VOICE: sparse angular supersaw line with a downward accelerate glide per bar.
d9 $ sometimesBy 0.25 (fast 2) $ n "<[~ ~ a4 ~ ~ e5 ~ ~] [~ c5 ~ ~ ~ ~ g4 ~] [~ ~ b4 ~ ~ ~ e5 ~] [~ ~ ~ d5 ~ ~ a4 ~]>" # s "supersaw" # orbit 3 # keyShift 0 # gain 0.46 # amp 0.5 # accelerate "<-0.03 0 -0.04 -0.02>" # attack 0.02 # release 0.8 # sustain 0.5 # hpf 250 # lpf 7000 # pan 0.58 # delaytime 0.1875 # lock 1 # delayfeedback 0 # ddSend 0 # verbSend 0.42 # room 0.70 # size 0.8 # verbT60 3.2 # verbDamp 0.5 # verbHp 300 # verbLow 0.2 # verbHigh 0.7 # verbTone 4200 # tape 0 # tapeHiss 0
-- d10 THE GLASS: one high supervibe bell every other bar, reversed every 11 cycles.
d10 $ every 11 (rev) $ n "<[~ ~ a5 ~] [~ ~ ~ ~] [~ ~ e5 ~] [~ ~ ~ ~]>" # s "supervibe" # orbit 3 # keyShift 0 # gain 0.34 # amp 0.5 # attack 0.01 # release 1.4 # sustain 0.8 # hpf 500 # lpf 11000 # pan 0.66 # delaytime 0.1875 # lock 1 # delayfeedback 0 # ddSend 0 # verbSend 0.42 # room 0.70 # size 0.8 # verbT60 3.2 # verbDamp 0.5 # verbHp 300 # verbLow 0.2 # verbHigh 0.7 # verbTone 4200 # tape 0 # tapeHiss 0
-- ORBIT 4 — PERCUSSION + TEXTURE through tape. Owner d11; tape/delay/verb config agree.
-- d11 THE MARSH: p93perc loop, sliced with two rotating orders, chopped, reversed every 7.
d11 $ every 7 (rev) $ sometimesBy 0.3 (chop 12) $ slice 8 "<0 2 4 6 1 3 5 7> <2 0 6 4 3 1 7 5>" $ loopAt 1 $ s "p93perc" # orbit 4 # gain 0.32 # amp 0.8 # release 0.2 # hpf 700 # lpf 15000 # cut 8 # pan "0.34 0.66" # delaytime 0.1875 # lock 1 # delayfeedback 0.22 # ddSend 0.16 # ddHp 700 # ddLp 5200 # ddDrive 0.06 # ddWow 0.05 # ddCross 0.6 # ddDuck 0.5 # verbSend 0.12 # room 0.40 # size 0.5 # verbT60 2.0 # verbDamp 0.4 # verbHp 300 # verbLow 0.2 # verbHigh 0.6 # verbTone 4000 # tape 0.28 # tapeWow 0.22 # tapeHf 6500 # tapeHiss 0.012
-- d12 THE GHOST VIBES: sprvibe files picked by `n`, doubled every 9 cycles, taped.
d12 $ every 9 (fast 2) $ n "<[14 ~ ~ 7 ~ 12 ~ 17] [15 ~ 8 ~ 11 ~ 16 ~]>" # s "sprvibe" # orbit 4 # keyShift 0 # gain 0.30 # amp 0.9 # begin 0 # end 1 # sustain 0.5 # release 0.4 # hpf 200 # lpf 9000 # pan "0.36 0.64" # delaytime 0.1875 # lock 1 # delayfeedback 0.22 # ddSend 0.16 # ddHp 700 # ddLp 5200 # ddDrive 0.06 # ddWow 0.05 # ddCross 0.6 # ddDuck 0.5 # verbSend 0.12 # room 0.40 # size 0.5 # verbT60 2.0 # verbDamp 0.4 # verbHp 300 # verbLow 0.2 # verbHigh 0.6 # verbTone 4000 # tape 0.28 # tapeWow 0.22 # tapeHf 6500 # tapeHiss 0.012
-- ORBIT 5 — SEND BURSTS + a silent reset clock. Owner d13 for the delay config; d14
-- repeats that config identically and forces every send back to zero.
-- d13 THE THROW: one reversed sprvibe swell on the last beat of each section; the
-- ddSend pattern holds send high for exactly one event, and feedback stays at 0.30.
d13 $ struct "~ ~ ~ t" $ s "sprvibe:31" # speed (-1) # begin 0.05 # end 0.45 # sustain 0.20 # orbit 5 # gain "<0!15 0.16 0!15 0.16 0!15 0.14 0!11 0.18 0!4>" # hpf 900 # lpf 7000 # pan "0.20 0.80" # delaytime 0.1875 # lock 1 # delayfeedback 0.30 # ddSend "<0!15 0.30 0!15 0.30 0!15 0.28 0!11 0.32 0!4>" # ddHp 800 # ddLp 5000 # ddDrive 0.12 # ddWow 0.08 # ddCross 0.60 # ddDuck 0.55 # verbSend 0.40 # room 0.85 # size 0.9 # verbT60 4.5 # verbDamp 0.5 # verbHp 320 # verbLow 0.2 # verbHigh 0.65 # verbTone 4200 # tape 0 # tapeHiss 0
-- d14 THE RESET CLOCK: gain 0, tiny silent slice, 16 events/cycle; keeps orbit 5's
-- delay settings pinned and returns ddSend/verbSend to zero (per-event sends only,
-- so it omits room/size/verbT60 and does not compete with the owner).
d14 $ s "h2ogmbd:2*16" # orbit 5 # gain 0 # begin 0 # end 0.01 # sustain 0.001 # delaytime 0.1875 # lock 1 # delayfeedback 0.30 # ddSend 0 # ddHp 800 # ddLp 5000 # ddDrive 0.12 # ddWow 0.08 # ddCross 0.60 # ddDuck 0.55 # verbSend 0 # tape 0 # tapeHiss 0
